+Diffusers worker tuning and performance checklist
+
+1) xFormers / memory-efficient attention
+ - Prefer to install a prebuilt xformers wheel for your CUDA version. Building xformers from source on GPU nodes can be slow and error-prone.
+ - Enable memory-efficient attention in diffusers/pipeline by passing `torch_dtype=torch.float16` and using `enable_xformers_memory_efficient_attention()` on UNet if available:
+
+    try:
+        pipe.unet.enable_xformers_memory_efficient_attention()
+    except Exception:
+        pass
+
+2) Attention slicing
+ - For large images or limited GPU memory, enable attention slicing:
+
+    try:
+        pipe.enable_attention_slicing()
+    except Exception:
+        pass
+
+3) Mixed precision
+ - Use fp16 on CUDA GPUs. Ensure model is loaded with `torch_dtype=torch.float16` and moved to device.
+ - Test numerical stability and quality at fp16.
+
+4) Tensor offload / DeepSpeed offload
+ - For larger models, consider DeepSpeed offload configs or accelerate with `device_map="auto"` and offload folder configured.
+ - Benchmark operator memory and switch to offload when memory pressure is high.
+
+5) Scheduler & sampler-level optimizations
+ - Use faster schedulers (e.g., DPMSolverMultistep) where quality is acceptable for fewer steps.
+ - Tune `num_inference_steps` for quality vs latency trade-offs.
+
+6) Batching & aggregator
+ - Use Redis-based aggregator (dynamic batching) to group small requests into a batch.
+ - Ensure the pipeline supports list-of-prompts input for batched inference (some pipelines accept this natively).
+
+7) GPU utilization
+ - Monitor p50/p95 latency and GPU utilization. Increase batch size if GPU utilization is low, but watch tail latency.
+ - Use separate node pools for interactive (low-latency) vs batch (high-throughput).
+
+8) Benchmarking
+ - Use provided benchmark scripts and measure p50/p95/p99, throughput, and GPU memory.
+ - Run scaling experiments with KEDA to tune min/max replicas.
+
+9) CI & reproducibility
+ - Record model, scheduler, seed, and full generation config in the evidence metadata for every sample to allow deterministic replay.
+
